instruction says \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\". That might mean include case_id and _case_nonce in the output. However the task description says \"Return only JSON-serializable values with the exact named fields.\" It doesn't specify required fields. Could add them. Possibly the expected output format is predefined? Given it's a programming challenge, they might expect exactly `{\"token_labels\": ..., \"retained_indices\": ...}`. The phrase \"preserve every source identifier\" might refer to preserving the mapping from word groups to tokens? But the returned values already have indices. I'll include case_id and nonce to be safe, but the function must not mutate case, and return a JSON-serializable object. I'll include them as extra keys.\n\nAlso note: \"Do not use Markdown code fences. Do not add a preamble, explanation, or trailing text.\" So we output exactly a JSON object with key \"implementation\".\n\nNow write the code. Use only standard library.\n\nPlan:\n\n- Check required fields exist.\n- Validate lengths and indices.\n- Create token_labels list of None.\n- For each word group:\n  - label = word_labels[i]\n  - for idx in word_tok_idx[i]:\n    - if idx <0 or >= token_count: raise ValueError\n    - if token_labels[idx] is not None: raise ValueError (\"overlap\")\n    - token_labels[idx] = label\n- After loop, check None in token_labels: if any, raise ValueError\n- Compute retained = [i for i, lbl in enumerate(token_labels) if lbl == 1]\n- Return dict with token_labels (list of ints), retained_indices (list of ints), case_id, _case_nonce.\n\nBut careful: token_labels should be integers, not None. So after validation, it's safe.\n\nNow the JSON string for implementation: need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes. We'll write the Python source as a string within JSON.\n\nI'll produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":922,"completion_tokens":1293,"total_tokens":2215,"prompt